note Source: cpython/Lib/json/decoder.py, JSONDecoder.decode (lines 353-362). Python, error handling.
note Return the Python representation of `s` (a str instance containing a JSON document).

type JSONDecoder
    note fields (object_hook, parse_float, strict, ...) omitted; only raw_decode is used here

note GAP: dynamic value type - Python returns `obj` of any type (dict, list, str, int, float, bool, None). The doc has no "any" type; a choice is declared instead, which is closed where the Python result is open (object_hook can return any object).
choice JsonValue
    JsonObject with members as a List of JsonMember
    JsonArray with elements as a List of JsonValue
    JsonString with text as Text
    JsonNumber with number as a Number
    JsonTrue
    JsonFalse
    JsonNull

type JsonMember
    field key as Text
    field value as a JsonValue

note JSONDecodeError carries msg, doc, pos (and derived lineno, colno).
note GAP: failure with a payload - `fails with` and `fail with` only show bare names. Python raises JSONDecodeError("Extra data", s, end) with a message, the document and a position. Invented: `fail with JSONDecodeError with msg "Extra data" and doc s and pos end`, borrowing the `with ... and ...` form of choice variants.
note UNCLEAR: whether a failure is a type that can be declared; written here as a type.
type JSONDecodeError
    field msg as Text
    field doc as Text
    field pos as a Nat

note WORKAROUND: tuple result - raw_decode returns (obj, end). The doc has no tuples or multiple results, so a record type is declared just to carry the pair.
type DecodeResult
    field obj as a JsonValue
    field end as a Nat

to raw_decode s from idx with decoder
    given s is Text
    given idx is a Nat
    given decoder is a JSONDecoder
    produces a DecodeResult
    fails with JSONDecodeError

note WHITESPACE is a module-level compiled regex `[ \t\n\r]*`; `.match(s, pos).end()` gives the index after the whitespace run.
to skip_whitespace s from pos
    given s is Text
    given pos is a Nat
    produces a Nat

note WORKAROUND: default argument used for speed - `_w=WHITESPACE.match` binds a global regex method as a default parameter so lookups are local. The doc has no default arguments and no first-class functions; the parameter is dropped and skip_whitespace is called directly. Callers that passed their own `_w` cannot be expressed.
note WORKAROUND: method and self - `decode` is a method; `self` becomes an explicit parameter `decoder`.
to decode s with decoder
    given s is Text
    given decoder is a JSONDecoder
    produces a JsonValue
    fails with JSONDecodeError

    let start be skip_whitespace s from 0
    let decoded be try raw_decode s from start with decoder
    let end be skip_whitespace s from end of decoded
    note UNCLEAR: `count of s` for the length of Text - the doc shows `count of` only on lists and `length` only in a refinement (`Text with length 1 through 100`).
    if end is not count of s
        fail with JSONDecodeError with msg "Extra data" and doc s and pos end
    give back obj of decoded
